    "text_sha256": "d3d156348af6c312c4e29ad7125b224b15fcdcfeaa73609918c740b39f60deba",
    "source_url": "",
    "original_summary": "Guinea’s representative congratulated the President of the General Assembly and praised the Secretary-General’s efforts before presenting the country’s recent progress. He reaffirmed his view that imported governance models not adapted to African realities have failed to meet people’s expectations, while emphasizing that Guinea now seeks to share concrete results rather than denounce others. Under its Constitution, Guinea has held direct presidential, legislative, and communal elections, established institutions financed by its own treasury, and conducted elections peacefully and transparently without external assistance. The Constitution promotes peaceful coexistence, local representation, peaceful transfers of power, and recognition of the country’s cultural, linguistic, and religious plurality. In less than three years, Guinea reports paving more than 1,000 kilometers of roads, completing the Simandou mining and infrastructure project, building schools and hospitals, constructing three aluminum refineries, and operating Africa’s largest gold refinery. Through the Simandou 2040 program, Guinea aims to use the project to advance infrastructure, agriculture, energy, education, and health over the next 15 years. The speaker stressed that youth need quality education, labor-market-oriented training through the Simandou Academy, and opportunities for employment and entrepreneurship. He called for governance and international partnerships tailored to each nation’s historical, social, and cultural realities, while affirming Guinea’s commitment to sovereignty, international law, the UN Charter, and mutually respectful cooperation.",
    "sentences": [
      {
        "id": "S001",
        "text": "Mr."
      },
      {
        "id": "S002",
        "text": "President of the 81st session of the General Assembly of the United Nations, Mr."
      },
      {
        "id": "S003",
        "text": "Secretary-General of the United Nations, Excellencies, ladies and gentlemen, heads of state and government, Excellencies, ladies and gentlemen, heads of delegation, ladies and gentlemen."
      },
      {
        "id": "S004",
        "text": "Mr."
      },
      {
        "id": "S005",
        "text": "President, at the outset, I wish to convey to you, on behalf of the sovereign people of the Republic of Guinea and our delegation, our warmest congratulations upon your election to the presidency of this 81st session of the General Assembly of the United Nations."
      },
      {
        "id": "S006",
        "text": "I cherish the hope that our proceedings, under your skillful stewardship, will allow the United Nations, our organization, to best address and meet the legitimate aspirations of the peoples of the world."
      },
      {
        "id": "S007",
        "text": "I also wish to applaud the continuous and consistent efforts of the Secretary-General, Mr."
      },
      {
        "id": "S008",
        "text": "António Guterres, at the helm of our United Nations."
      },
      {
        "id": "S009",
        "text": "It is with a profound feeling of pride and humility that I speak before this august body on behalf of the sovereign people of the Republic of Guinea, as we seek to describe to the international community the progress that my country has achieved."
      },
      {
        "id": "S010",
        "text": "Ladies and gentlemen, three years ago, from this rostrum, I spoke with the candor to which my country and our continent are bound."
      },
      {
        "id": "S011",
        "text": "I spoke the truth, and I stated that the model of imported governance, without being adapted to our continent, was not generating the fruits that had been expected by our peoples."
      },
      {
        "id": "S012",
        "text": "This is something which I stand by."
      },
      {
        "id": "S013",
        "text": "But today, I am once again speaking before you with a different mindset."
      },
      {
        "id": "S014",
        "text": "I do not seek to denounce, but rather to share with you factual elements about the progress and headway that have been made by the Republic of Guinea, as we have achieved results that have emanated from the choices that we have made."
      },
      {
        "id": "S015",
        "text": "On the basis of our Constitution, the Republic of Guinea organized entirely direct presidential, legislative, and communal elections, and we have established all institutions, which are entirely financed by our treasury."
      },
      {
        "id": "S016",
        "text": "I state this with a rightful sense of pride: none of these elections, which were held throughout our territory, were marred by any significant incidents on the part of any of the participants in this electoral process."
      },
      {
        "id": "S017",
        "text": "This reflects the fact, ladies and gentlemen, that a country can independently organize, using its own resources, credible, peaceful, and transparent elections."
      },
      {
        "id": "S018",
        "text": "This Constitution that we have adopted introduces profound innovations in terms of peaceful coexistence, as well as greater representation of our localities and communities, novel guarantees for the peaceful transfer of power, and recognition of our cultural, linguistic, religious, and cultural plurality as the bedrock of our nation and not as a divisive factor."
      },
      {
        "id": "S019",
        "text": "This I state with a sense of legitimate pride."
      },
      {
        "id": "S020",
        "text": "All of these elections were organized on our soil, once again, without any assistance from any party whatsoever."
      },
      {
        "id": "S021",
        "text": "Ladies and gentlemen, I did not come here to engage in rhetoric, but I do believe it is worthwhile to share with you a simple overview and useful information about what the Republic of Guinea has achieved in less than three years."
      },
      {
        "id": "S022",
        "text": "We have paved more than a thousand kilometers of roads, which have connected our regions."
      },
      {
        "id": "S023",
        "text": "We have the Simandou mega-project, Africa's largest mining and infrastructure project, which is currently complete."
      },
      {
        "id": "S024",
        "text": "We have schools and hospitals that have been built throughout the Republic of Guinea."
      },
      {
        "id": "S025",
        "text": "We have three aluminum refineries under construction, as we seek to transform our bauxite on our own soil."
      },
      {
        "id": "S026",
        "text": "We have Africa's largest gold refinery, which is currently operational and has already been completed."
      },
      {
        "id": "S027",
        "text": "We have a sustainable and responsible socioeconomic development program for my country for the next 15 years, which I refer to as the Simandou 2040 project."
      },
      {
        "id": "S028",
        "text": "The Simandou 2040 program embodies a transformation initiative for our economy."
