        "id": "S037",
        "text": "Let us consider certain nations in the Middle East."
      },
      {
        "id": "S038",
        "text": "They did not wait for an external model to be endorsed in order to become prosperous."
      },
      {
        "id": "S039",
        "text": "They drew inspiration from universal experience, while at the same time tailoring that to their national brilliance."
      },
      {
        "id": "S040",
        "text": "In one generation, they managed to achieve what others spent a century attaining."
      },
      {
        "id": "S041",
        "text": "Africa too can embark upon this path."
      },
      {
        "id": "S042",
        "text": "This is not reflective of a rejection of the world, nor a rejection of international cooperation."
      },
      {
        "id": "S043",
        "text": "Quite to the contrary, this is a call for win-win partnership, a partnership that is respectful of the sovereignty of each nation, rooted in win-win collaboration rather than pre-established arrangements which disregard our realities."
      },
      {
        "id": "S044",
        "text": "The Republic of Guinea, for our part, is and shall remain a reliable, open, and engaged partner vis-à-vis the international community, while engaging in mutual respect for the sovereignty of one and all."
      },
      {
        "id": "S045",
        "text": "Mr."
      },
      {
        "id": "S046",
        "text": "President, Excellencies, ladies and gentlemen, the Republic of Guinea is advancing."
      },
      {
        "id": "S047",
        "text": "We are making headway by harnessing our own means, by capitalizing upon our own choices for the benefit of our own people, and we are doing so in a manner that is in accordance with international law, with the spirit of the Charter of the United Nations, and in the spirit of candid and inclusive cooperation with all of our partners."
      },
      {
        "id": "S048",
        "text": "I cherish the hope that this Guinean experience can, to a modest degree, stimulate more in-depth consideration of the manifold legitimate development pathways for our continent."
